  "exportedAt": "2026-09-27T14:17:41.7067291+00:00",
  "messages": [
    {
      "id": "1553488070605537442",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-26T19:26:58.445+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Hi all. I'm designing a half-height (1x0p5) chip for Run 3 with the 3.3 V core (as_sc_mcu7t3v3 + ocd_io). It uses two eFuse macros from Egor's compiler. Egor's Run 1 report says writes are only reliable at 5 V (~15 mA/bit), while reads work at 3.3 V. So I'd like to give the eFuses their own supply segment:\n- Two `gf180mcu_ocd_io__brk5` cells on the west side isolate the last six pads: analog 3..0, DVSS 6 and DVDD 6.\n- DVDD 6 goes to the eFuse voltage (<= 5.0 V while programming), and analog 0 carries VDD_EFUSE into the core.\n- No template power/ground pad is removed or moved. Only DVDD 6's voltage and the two break cells change. VSS stays continuous, since brk5 only carries VSS.\n\nQuestions:\n1. Will precheck accept a pad ring modified this way (break cells, one DVDD pad at a different voltage)? Is there any rule on a minimum number of DVDD/DVSS pads per segment?\n2. On the Run 1 1x0p5 CoB board, DVDD 6 (bond pad 61) is on its own net `PWR_AUX_1`, and analog 0 (pad 63) is separate too. Will the Run 3 half-slot carrier keep that arrangement?\n3. Leo, I noticed you added eFuses to one of your 3.3 V designs and then took them out about two weeks later. Was that for a supply, DRC/precheck or area reason? Anything I should watch out for?\n\nI've also emailed info@wafer.space with the board-voltage part of this, and asked Egor about 3.3 V operation on the compiler's GitHub (egorxe/gf180_efuse_compiler#1). Posting here too in case the answers help others. Thanks!",
      "author": {
        "id": "693749740961267742",
        "name": "sriharshapy",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "heathcliff",
        "color": null,
