      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "> I'm planning on making an analog pad that allows analog voltage input higher than VIO, exactly so you can feed voltage inside without needing to have the VIO be 5V or break the ring.\n\n@tnt Cool, thanks! Will it be something like the current analog pad but without the ESD clamps or something more complex?\n\n> We have an io library with separate VDD and DVDD already btw.\n\nYou mean the ocd_io where core & IO voltage are separated, right? I've actually meant not this, but having two independent core voltage rails within the pad ring and for example clamping the digital pads to one of them and analog to another. That would allow using different supplies for the digital and analog domain if needed without breaking the ring, but requires a lot of work obviously.",
